arges when applicable -- matches \"if cursed, both surcharges apply\"\n25. should have 100 G deductible per damage event -- matches \"A deductible of 100 G applies per damage event\" and example: 500 G damage to regular sword → payout 400 G\"\n26. should cap total payout per policy at twice the insurance sum -- matches \"The total payout per policy is capped at twice the insurance sum\" and example: sword insured (cap 2000 G); two claims of 1500 G each → second claim reduced to 600 G\"\n27. should reimburse 50 % of damage amount for items with enchantment level ≥ 8 -- matches \"Damage to items with enchantment level ≥ 8 is reimbursed at 50 % of the damage amount\"\n28. should fully reimburse damage to items made of dragon material -- matches \"Damage to items made of dragon material is fully reimbursed\"\n29. should apply high-enchantment clause (50 % reimbursement) rather than dragon material clause for dragon-material item with enchantment ≥ 8 -- matches example: dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G (50 % rule wins, then deductible)\n30. should apply dragon material clause (full reimbursement) for dragon-material item with enchantment < 8 -- matches example: dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G → payout 700 G (full reimbursement, then deductible)\n31. should apply 50 % rule for non-dragon item with enchantment ≥ 8 -- matches example: steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G (50 % first, then deductible)\n32. should process two separate damages for two swords insured under policy -- matches \"a policy covers two swords → ... each entry is treated as a separate damage with its own deductible\"\n33. should reject claim when damages list includes item not covered by policy -- matches \"if the `damages` array contains more entries of a given type than the policy actually covers → whole claim rejected\"\n34. should reject claim when damage entry has invalid amount (e.g. negative) -- matches \"claim contains damage entry with `amount: -200` → CLI exits with non-zero status\"\n35. should use unmodified insurance value to calculate policy cap (premium modifiers do not raise cap) -- matches \"a cursed sword (insurance value 1000 G, premium with modifiers 165 G) → cap 2000 G (based on unmodified insurance value)\"\n36. should calculate insurance sum as sum of items' insurance values, even for components -- matches \"a policy covers a sword and 3 runes (a block) → insurance sum 1750 G (= 1000 + 3×250); the block discount affects the premium only, not the insurance sum\"\n37. should reject quote for unknown item type (e.g. broomstick) -- matches \"quote includes an item with an unknown type → the CLI exits with non-zero status\"\n38. should reject claim for item not part of the policy -- matches \"claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy → the CLI exits with non-zero status\"\n39. should round final premium up in MHPCO's favor (e.g. 197.5 G → 198 G) -- matches \"only the final premium or payout is rounded\" and \"rounded up\"\"\n40. should round final payout down in MHPCO's favor (e.g. 350.5 G → 350 G)"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784950529989,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8dbb8231-2045-4d5a-83e4-dd5c7e40a32b","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Test List\n\nTest List Created:\n**Feature**: MHPCO Claim Office - quote and claim processing\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 41\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should return 5 G premium for empty item list -- matches \"empty item list → premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\"\n2. should return 100 G base premium for a sword -- matches \"Sword